L000292	\section{End Matter}
L000293	Though our main focus has been on the control transition itself, we can examine generic properties of the controlled phase using both distributions obtained from the Fokker-Planck analysis and exact quantum channel results of the IHO.
L000294	
L000295	In \cref{fig:powerlaw}, we compare the power-law form of $\mathcal{Q}_+(\sigma_+)$ in \cref{eq:powerlawQ} to the distribution computed numerically for $p>p_c$.
L000296	The lower boundary of the FP dynamics is vital for the existence of a late-time steady state in the controlled phase---in \cref{eq:FP0} $\bar{v}<0$ for $p>p_c$, so the distribution drifts to small $y$ and is held up by the barrier at $y^\mathrm{min}$.
L000297	These two opposing forces balance to yield a stable distribution.
L000298	
L000299	We can further compute moments of this distribution
L000300	\begin{equation}
L000301	    \overline{\sigma_+^n} = \int\dd\sigma_+ \sigma_+^n\mathcal{Q}_+(\sigma_+) = \frac{2^{-\xi}\xi}{\xi-n},
L000302	\end{equation}
L000303	and find that the $n$th moment of $\sigma_+$ is finite only when $\xi>n$.
L000304	Setting $\xi = n$ gives a sequence of control rates at which these moments become finite in the FP framework,
L000305	\begin{equation} \label{eq:pFP}
L000306	    p^\mathrm{FP}_{2n} = p_c + (1-p_c)n\kappa + O(\kappa^2) > p_c,
L000307	\end{equation}
L000308	where we have expanded the result in small $\kappa$ since this was necessary to obtain \cref{eq:FP0} and $\mathcal{Q}_+(\sigma_+)$.
L000309	The $n$th moment of $\mathcal{Q}_+$ is related to quantum operators of order $2n$ since $\sigma_+$ is quadratic.
L000310	
L000311	\begin{figure}[h]
L000312	    \centering
L000313	    \includegraphics[width=0.8\columnwidth]{powerlaw_fig.pdf}
L000314	    \caption{Comparison of the power-law form of the distribution $\mathcal{Q}_+(\sigma_+)$ acquired from the FP analysis with the distribution of $\sigma_+$ computed numerically from the fixed point of $\mathbb{T}$ with $\kappa = \gamma = 0.2$ and cutoff $L=50$ for $p=0.6$.}
L000315	    \label{fig:powerlaw}
L000316	\end{figure}
L000317	
L000318	This sequence of moment control rates are directly related to the sequence of control rates $p^\ast$ in \cref{eq:pstar} for which quantum operators of order $n$ become controlled: $p^\ast_{2n} = p^\mathrm{FP}_{2n}$ to first order in $\kappa$.
L000319	This confirms that the FP analysis captures key features of the exact quantum dynamics in the appropriate limits, and equivalently demonstrates that the operators $\hat{Z}_{n}$ generalize the moment-control picture of the semiclassical analysis to a quantum context.
